<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Global Maven settings for the CI build image (copied to conf/settings.xml by
    the Dockerfile). These apply to EVERY Maven invocation in the container,
    including the child builds started by maven-invoker-plugin — a child's own
    `-s <settings>` replaces the *user* settings but not these.

    Deliberately declares NO remote snapshot repository.

    The build produces every org.mock-server SNAPSHOT it consumes, and nothing in
    the reactor depends on a third-party SNAPSHOT, so central-portal-snapshots can
    only ever return our own artifacts from an earlier build. Declaring it makes
    Maven merge its maven-metadata.xml with the locally installed one and take the
    newest lastUpdated, which risks:

      * false red — an unnecessary hard network dependency; a failed fetch
        (Sonatype outage, or a TLS-inspection proxy holding a .jar for sandbox
        analysis and answering 403) fails the reactor in an unrelated module long
        after that module's own tests passed; and
      * false green — whenever the locally installed snapshot is OLDER than the
        last published one, the remote wins and the test verifies a previously
        published build instead of the code under test.

    This pipeline runs `clean install` over the whole reactor before any
    integration test, and deploys the snapshot only after the build (behind a
    `wait` in .buildkite/pipeline-java.yml), so the just-installed copy is normally
    the newer one and CI is not expected to have hit either mode. It was still a
    latent hazard here: these settings apply to every Maven process in the
    container, so it would take effect the moment a module was skipped, a partial
    reactor was built, or the ordering changed.

    Consuming a MockServer snapshot from OUTSIDE this repository is documented in
    README.md and jekyll-www.mock-server.com/where/maven_central.html; that is a
    user-side repository declaration, not a build-side one.
-->
<settings xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd">
</settings>
